1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
OpenBox Shift-Left — the whole developer journey, end to end

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Install → onboard → sync rules → run Claude Code → lineage in the dashboard

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Step 1 — install: build the one static engine and put `openbox` on PATH

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Step 2 — `openbox dev init`: reuses my agent, installs the Claude Code plugin + hooks

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Credentials, config, and the commit-trailer git hook are all set by onboarding

6
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Step 3 — `openbox dev sync`: the enforcement rules are pulled from the backend

7
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:18,000
No hand-written policy — the bundle is whatever the org configured server-side

8
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Step 4 — start the local sidecar; it loads that synced policy bundle

9
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Now just run Claude Code — governance is ambient from here

10
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Prompt: create config.env with fake AWS + GitHub credentials

11
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:06,000
TIER 1 · local secret redaction — in-process, before anything leaves the machine

12
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:18,000
The file on disk shows ${OPENBOX_REDACTED_…} — the real keys never egressed

13
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Prompt: run a risky shell install (curl … | bash)

14
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:46,000
TIER 2 · advisory approval — the synced policy asks before a high-risk command runs

15
00:02:46,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Honest limit: client-side hooks run on MY machine — I can approve this locally…

16
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:12,000
…so it's deterrence + a tamper-evident record, not a hard block. Every choice is logged.

17
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:24,000
New session — TIER 3 · async guardrail findings surfaced back into the chat

18
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:38,000
A code change + commit — the hook stamps OpenBox-Session: <run-id>

19
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Deploy — the git-action emits a Deploy event; lineage: commit → session → deploy

20
00:03:52,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Now the HARD gate — paste a real AWS key into a prompt…

21
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:20,000
…the SERVER-SIDE secrets guardrail HALTS the session — no local "accept" can override it

22
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:32,000
That's the line: advisory at the dev's hands, enforced where the dev holds no keys

23
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:45,000
The UAT dashboard — every action recorded: redaction, the approval, the HALT

24
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Merkle leaves sealed — tamper-evident; and the commit→session→deploy lineage

25
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Shift-left: default-on governance + an audit trail you can't quietly bypass
